/P 471 0 R
/E (Health and wellness councils are community bodies that advise and support the Tennessee Department of Health regarding the health and social needs in their county.1 In this role, the Rutherford County Wellness Council leads community health improvement efforts in partnership with state and local health departments, nonprofit hospitals, community clinics, colleges and universities, and nonprofits. This includes a Community Health Assessment \(CHA\) every three years to better understand the state of health and social factors influencing the health of Rutherford County, and prioritize top needs \(Figure 1\). Action steps to drive change and improve the prioritized needs are outlined in the Community Health Improvement Plan \(CHIP\).1)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [4 6 5 1208 0 R]
>>
endobj
