592 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 471 0 R
/E (The Rutherford County 2022-2025 CHIP covers five public health needs: Healthcare Access, Mental Health, Opioid Use, Safe and Affordable Housing, and Infant Mortality \(see Figure 2\). The Wellness Council has a workgroup that leads the actions for each prioritized health needs in the CHIP. This report is one of the actions named in the CHIP for the infant mortality workgroup. The goal of the report is raising awareness about local data, evidenced-based practices, and community resources that support infant wellness.1)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [8 1209 0 R]
>>
