/T (Data Story Within all child deaths \(17 years old and younger\) that occurred and were  reviewed by TN Child Fatality Review Teams in 2023, the majority \(51%\) were  for Infants \(< 1 year of age\). The rate of infant mortality across the state was  6.5 deaths per 1,000 live births, 16.1% higher than the national rate of 5.6 deaths  per 1,000 live births. TDH reports infant mortality rates over 5 years to observe trends  over time. Since 2019, the infant mortality rate decreased by 7.1% from 7 deaths per 1,000 live  births. Regionally, Mid-Cumberland, which surrounds Nashville-Davidson County and includes Rutherford  County, has not experienced statistically significant changes in Infant Mortality Rates year over year between 2019-2023.18 Within the same years in Rutherford County, the infant mortality rate ranged from 4.4 to 7.5 deaths per 1,000 live births, with the spike from the lowest rate to the highest rate between 2020 and 2021. Since 2022, the infant mortality rate has improved in Rutherford County. Additionally, the  difference in how communities experience infant  mortalityoutcomes has narrowed in 2023 and  2024. Even in the year \(2020\) with the lowest  rate, the infant mortality rate for Black infants  was 2.8x higher than for White infants.17 )
/E (Data Story Within all child deaths \(17 years old and younger\) that occurred and were  reviewed by TN Child Fatality Review Teams in 2023, the majority \(51%\) were  for Infants \(< 1 year of age\). The rate of infant mortality across the state was  6.5 deaths per 1,000 live births, 16.1% higher than the national rate of 5.6 deaths  per 1,000 live births. TDH reports infant mortality rates over 5 years to observe trends  over time. Since 2019, the infant mortality rate decreased by 7.1% from 7 deaths per 1,000 live  births. Regionally, Mid-Cumberland, which surrounds Nashville-Davidson County and includes Rutherford  County, has not experienced statistically significant changes in Infant Mortality Rates year over year between 2019-2023.18 Within the same years in Rutherford County, the infant mortality rate ranged from 4.4 to 7.5 deaths per 1,000 live births, with the spike from the lowest rate to the highest rate between 2020 and 2021. Since 2022, the infant mortality rate has improved in Rutherford County. Additionally, the  difference in how communities experience infant  mortalityoutcomes has narrowed in 2023 and  2024. Even in the year \(2020\) with the lowest  rate, the infant mortality rate for Black infants  was 2.8x higher than for White infants.17 )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [10 1234 0 R 11 13 15 14]
>>
