/P 2514 0 R
/E (Consideration: Differences in what is considered a top cause when comparing CFR data and Vital Stats data can also be contributed to differences in the cause identification process. The cause of death through the CFR process is informed by various records and involves an in-depth local review, which can be somewhat subjective depending on the reviewers of each case. Additionally, the cause of death categories on death certificates are based on ICD-10 codes, while the categories in the CFR database are derived from those available in the National Center for Fatality Review Case Reporting System.18)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [21 1259 0 R]
