972 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 481 0 R
/E (Topic: Standard and emerging best practices for parent/caregiver education around safe sleep practices in infants.  )
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
973 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 481 0 R
/T (Introduction  )
/E (Introduction  )
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
974 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 481 0 R
/E (Ensuring the safety and well-being of infants during sleep is a critical concern for public health professionals. Safe sleep practices are essential to reduce the risk of sudden unexpected infant death \(SUID\) and other sleep-related infant deaths. Various standard and emerging practices have been developed to educate parents and caregivers on how to create a safe sleep environment for infants. Standard best practices typically include recommendations from the American Academy of Pediatrics, which emphasize placing infants on their backs to sleep, using a firm sleep surface, and keeping soft bedding and toys out of the crib.  )
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
975 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 481 0 R
/E (Emerging best practices focus on leveraging new technologies and community-based interventions to further improve education and adherence to safe sleep recommendations. By examining both standard and emerging practices, additional strategies can be implemented to improve preventable infant deaths due to unsafe sleep events.  )
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
976 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 481 0 R
/T (Establishing strong relationships between healthcare providers and caregivers significantly enhances infant health outcomes.    )
/E (Establishing strong relationships between healthcare providers and caregivers significantly enhances infant health outcomes.    )
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
977 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 481 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [8 12 9 13 10 14 11 15]
>>
endobj
978 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 481 0 R
/T (Incorporating a health education component and providing safe sleep spaces for infants are essential elements in the development of effective SUID prevention programs.   )
/E (Incorporating a health education component and providing safe sleep spaces for infants are essential elements in the development of effective SUID prevention programs.   )
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
