1027 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 484 0 R
/E (Any resource meeting these criteria was deemed eligible for inclusion in the asset mapping process. This systematic approach ensured that the final map accurately represented the landscape of maternal and infant health resources available within Rutherford County, providing valuable insights for stakeholders and decision-makers. )
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
1028 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 484 0 R
/T (Findings   )
/E (Findings   )
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
1029 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 484 0 R
/E (Data Compilation and Organization )
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
1030 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 484 0 R
/E (All qualifying entries identified during the search process were documented and organized in a spreadsheet. This spreadsheet included essential information such as addresses, website URLs, and contact details for each resource. Additionally, efforts were made to enhance the comprehensiveness of the dataset by identifying and categorizing content and functional areas for each resource. )
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
1031 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 484 0 R
/E (Functional Areas )
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
1032 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 484 0 R
/E (Functional areas were identified to provide a comprehensive understanding of the services offered by each resource. These areas were determined according to the levels of service outlined in the Maternal and Child Health Pyramid of Health Services.34 The model serves as a framework for understanding the continuum of care provided to mothers and children, encompassing preventive, primary, and specialized services. Functional areas were categorized based on the specific roles and functions of each resource within this framework, providing insights into the breadth and depth of maternal and infant health services available within Rutherford County. )
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [7 1261 0 R 8 10]
>>
endobj
1033 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Span
/K [9]
/Pg 27 0 R
/P 1261 0 R
>>
endobj
1034 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 484 0 R
/E (Content Areas )
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
1035 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 484 0 R
/E (Content areas were identified to delineate the scope of services covered by each resource. These areas were derived from an abbreviated selection sourced from Healy et al., which offers a comprehensive listing of maternal and infant health services.35 Content areas included a wide range of domains, including prenatal care, childbirth education, postpartum support, infant feeding assistance, and pediatric care. By identifying content areas, the report seeks to provide a more nuanced understanding of the diverse array of services available to families with infants within Rutherford County and make it easier to identify gaps and provide recommendations. )
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [12 1262 0 R 13 15]
>>
endobj
1036 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Span
/K [14]
/Pg 27 0 R
/P 1262 0 R
>>
endobj
1037 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 484 0 R
/E (Limitations )
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
1038 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 484 0 R
/E (The community asset map may not offer a complete representation of available resources due to the exclusion of certain assets that did not meet the predetermined inclusion criteria. Additionally, valuable resources that failed to meet specific criteria will not be visually represented on the map. Furthermore, while the map primarily focuses on resources directly located within the community of interest, it also includes resources that serve the broader regional area. Resources located outside the immediate vicinity may not be as easily accessible to community members. Additionally, the information provided on the map for each resource includes website details where available. )
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [17]
>>
endobj
1039 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 484 0 R
/E (Users should be aware of these limitations and understand that the map may not provide a complete picture of available resources. Therefore, a disclaimer will be included on the map, advising users to reference the accompanying resource list for a comprehensive overview. )
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [18]
>>
endobj
